hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"102","Bismika rabbi wada'tu janbi, wa bika arfa'uhu, fa-in amsakta nafsī farhamhā, wa-in arsaltahā fahfazhā bimā tahfazu bihi 'ibādaka aṣ-ṣāliḥīn.. In Your name, my Lord, I lay down my side, and by You I raise it. If You take my soul, have mercy on it, and if You release it, then protect it as You protect Your righteous servants."
"103","Allāhumma innaka khalaqta nafsī wa anta tawaffāhā, laka mamātuhā wa mahyāhā, in aḥyaytahā faḥfazhā, wa in amattahā faghfir lahā. Allāhumma innī as'aluka al-ʿāfiyah.. O Allah, You created my soul and You will take it to Yourself; its death and its life belong to You. If You grant it life, protect it, and if You cause it to die, forgive it. O Allah, I ask You for well-being."
